# user_stories.txt
#
# This file serves as a simple, text-based database to store user stories for a GIF generation project.
# It's structured with each user story occupying a set of lines, organized as key-value pairs for easy parsing.
#
# Each user story represents a desired feature, animation frame, or functionality.
# It is used to provide specific and measurable goals for the project.
#
# Format:
# - Each user story is broken into the following fields:
#   - ID: (Integer) A unique identifier for each user story.
#   - User Story: (String) The user story in the "As a...I want...So that..." format.
#   - Description: (String) A detailed description of the animation frame generated by a model (e.g., Gemini).
#   - Tags: (String, comma-separated) Keywords for searching and categorizing user stories.
#   - Status: (String) Tracks the completion status of the user story (e.g., Pending, In Progress, Done).
#
# Notes:
# - It's advised to keep user stories well-defined and focused to ensure the scope is clear.
# - In more complex projects, a more robust database or system is typically used.
# - The tags should be kept consistent and representative to maximize the power of the tagging system.

